  "details": "I noticed that OCS playback automatically enables Flying and anchors the camera to the world, even when I disable those settings in the JSON. Because of this, recorded roll/tilt doesn't playback correctly in VR.\n\nInterestingly, this isn't an issue on desktop. When recording camera samples and using the camera's Rotate button, the rotation/roll is recorded and plays back correctly.\n\nThe only workaround I've found in VR is converting the samples to the Dolly system, but it reduces 865 samples to 100, which is very limiting.\n\nIt would be great if VR OCS playback could properly reproduce the recorded camera rotation/roll and respect the camera's Flying/anchoring settings.",
